# Gate: a converged SCF must not be blocked by DIIS roundoff noise.
#
# is_converged() also gates on the DIIS residual FPS-SPF, to reject a stalled
# step whose density happens to repeat (see he_sad_ccpvdz). That gate used to
# compare the residual against tol_density -- but the two quantities have
# different numerical floors. dP is a difference of densities and reaches
# exactly 0; FPS-SPF is a product of converged matrices and bottoms out in
# roundoff, then wanders there. Measured on this system at iteration 430:
# dP_max = 2.1e-15 (machine precision) while diis_error read 6.9e-13 and kept
# drifting over 1e-12..8e-10 for another thousand iterations.
#
# So any tol_density below the DIIS noise floor made convergence unreachable
# by construction: this exact input used to exhaust max_cycles and report
# failure while sitting exactly on the solution. No other regression case uses
# a tolerance this tight, which is why the defect survived.
%begin_control
    basis       sto-3g
    calculation energy
    verbosity   normal
    basis_type  cartesian
%end_control

%begin_scf
    scf_type    uhf
    use_diis    .true.
    diis_dim    8
    engine      os
    guess       hcore
    max_cycles  200
    tol_energy  1.0e-12
    tol_density 1.0e-12
%end_scf

%begin_geom
    coord_type  cartesian
    coord_units angstrom
    use_symm    .false.
%end_geom

%begin_coords
4
1 2
O 0.000 0.717 -0.041
O 0.021 -0.717 0.032
H 0.851 0.887 0.463
H -0.802 -0.911 0.395
%end_coords
